Copyright (c) 2026 David Petry
https://davidpetry-cloud.github.io/drum-studio/

Drum Studio was conceived, designed and directed by David Petry and built
with the help of AI tools (Claude Code). David Petry offers it under the
licences below, to the full extent of the rights he holds in it.

In short: you are welcome to use, share, learn from and build on Drum
Studio for any noncommercial purpose, as long as you credit David Petry.
Commercial use needs his written permission.


1. Which licence covers what
----------------------------

CODE: PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
  Everything that makes the app work: dart/, js/, css/, sw.js,
  manifest.webmanifest, .github/, and the markup (the HTML structure) of
  index.html and tuning.html. Parts of js/ that come from third parties
  keep their own licences (section 5).
  Full text: LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.txt
  Online:    https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0

CONTENT: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
(CC BY-NC 4.0)
  The words and visuals: the text on the pages, the tuning guide's
  descriptions and advice (including the text inside
  dart/lib/tuning_data.dart), the README and other documentation, the
  visual design, and the graphics and icons in icons/.
  Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt
  Online:    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

Where content sits inside a code file, the content licence covers the
content and the code licence covers the code.


2. How to credit David Petry
----------------------------

Code: the PolyForm licence requires you to pass on this line with any
copy of any part of the code, including changed versions:

Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2026 David Petry (https://davidpetry-cloud.github.io/drum-studio/)

Content: CC BY-NC 4.0 requires you to name the creator, link to the
licence, and say whether you made changes. For example:

  Based on "Drum Studio" by David Petry
  (https://davidpetry-cloud.github.io/drum-studio/), licensed under
  CC BY-NC 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).
  Changes: [what you changed].

Where practical, please also credit David Petry wherever your work is
shown, such as an About page, a credits screen or a description.


3. Commercial use
-----------------

Anything these licences don't permit, including selling Drum Studio or
work based on it, or using it to earn money, needs David Petry's prior
written permission. For a commercial licence, contact him through
https://david-petry.netlify.app/.


4. Names and logo
-----------------

Neither licence grants any right to use the names "Drum Studio" or
"David Petry" or the Drum Studio logo, except to give the credit in
section 2. Please don't use them in a way that suggests David Petry made
or endorses your version.


5. Third-party components
-------------------------

The fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1) and the Dart runtime compiled into
js/ (BSD 3-Clause) are not covered by this file. They keep their own
licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.


6. Contributions
----------------

If you send a change to this project (for example, a pull request), you
confirm you have the right to do so, and you license your change to
David Petry under the same licences as the part of the project it
changes. You also permit David Petry to offer Drum Studio, including your
change, under other terms, such as a commercial licence.


7. No warranty
--------------

Drum Studio is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, as set out
in both licences. Pitch ranges and tuning advice are general starting
points gathered from the published sources listed in the app. They are
not guarantees about any particular instrument.
